```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate RPO/RTO during drills without impacting production SAP?
- What metrics and logs would you centralize for audit and post-DR learning?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of AWS patching automation, SAP patching options, health checks, rollback strategies, and CloudFormation for operational guardrails.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Maintenance Windows
- SAP patching options: SUM vs OS patches
- Pre/post patch validation: SAPControl, SAP background jobs, host metrics
- Rollback strategies: SAP backups, AMI snapshots
- CloudFormation for roles and patch baselines

## Code Example
```javascript
// CFN skeleton (pseudo)
{
  "AWSTemplateFormatVersion": "2010-09-09",
  "Resources": {
    "SAPSSMRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": { "Version": "2012-10-17", "Statement": [ { "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": { "Service": ["ec2.amazonaws.com", "ssm.amazonaws.com"] }, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole" } ] },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": [ "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMFullAccess" ]
      }
    },
    "SAPPatchBaseline": {
      "Type": "AWS::SSM::PatchBaseline",
      "Properties": {
        "Name": "SAPBaseline",
        "OperatingSystem": "AmazonLinux2"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify patch success in SAP and the OS without impacting production?
- How would you extend to multi-region DR alignment and scoped approvals?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical data protection across SAP on AWS with Snowflake analytics, balancing real-time access and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- SAP S/4HANA data ingestion and masking
- Field-level masking rules for PII
- Snowflake masking policies and data sharing
- AWS KMS key management and IAM governance
- Auditing, rollback, and failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example masking function
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{2}).+(@.*)/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.replace(/(\d{3})\d{4}(\d{3})/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-' + r.ssn.slice(-4);
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate masking without leaking data in logs?
- How would you rotate keys and propagate policy changes across Snowflake without downtime?
